                                    <signatures>
                                        The six quaternions containing the Acts of the Apostles are indicated on the inner upper corner of the first or last folio of the quire with Ethiopic numerals from ፩ to ፮ (so that the first quaternion is marked on the first folio only, the second on the last folio only, the third on the last folio only, and so on).
                                        The last four quires containing the conclusion of the Pauline Epistles are indicated on the inner upper corner of the first or last folio of the quire with Ethiopic numerals from ፲፩ to ፲፬.
                                    </signatures>
                                    <note>
                                        According to the catalogue, the manuscript consists of a binion, six quaternion, a bifolium, ten quaternions (the last two leaves of the tenth quaternion have been cut off and placed at the beginning as guardleaves), other two quaternions, one ternion, and one sextern. However, the total number of leaves thus calculated is 168, while the total number of leaves indicated by the cataloguers is 170.
                                    </note>
                                </collation>
